# macOS
.DS_Store

# Build output — built locally, published by the manager at /dist, never committed
dist/
dist.new/
dist.old/
bin/
*.exe
*.test
*.out

# Local runtime state
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
.nsm/

# Editor
.idea/
.vscode/

# SDD scratch workspace
.superpowers/

# iCloud conflict copies. This repo lives under ~/Documents, which macOS syncs to
# iCloud; when a sync races a checkout, copies named "<name> 2.<ext>" appear. A .go
# copy inside a package is COMPILED BY GO whether or not git tracks it, so it
# redeclares live symbols and the build fails with errors that look like real
# defects. It has happened twice here (34 files each time, byte-identical).
#
# What each layer buys, because they are not interchangeable:
#   - these patterns stop `git add -A` from COMMITTING a half-merged duplicate,
#     which would break CI for every clone and not just this machine;
#   - scripts/check-tree.sh catches the duplicate PRESENT IN THE TREE, which git
#     ignoring it does nothing about. `make test` runs the guard first.
#
# Every numeric suffix, not just " 2": b10coincom's history has a " 2"-only rule
# that missed a " 3.go", which was then committed and failed staticcheck in CI.
* [0-9]
* [0-9].go
* [0-9].md
* [0-9].sh
* [0-9].sql
* [0-9].json
* [0-9].txt
* [0-9].yml
* [0-9].yaml
* [0-9].toml
* [0-9].mod
* [0-9].sum
